WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.800 --> 00:00:04.246
IF is the first logic function every analyst needs.

2
00:00:04.246 --> 00:00:09.607
In this lesson, you will learn the three parts of IF, write your first

3
00:00:09.607 --> 00:00:14.968
IF column to label cancelled orders, and check the result with a quick filter.

4
00:00:14.968 --> 00:00:16.500
Let's add some logic!

5
00:00:18.400 --> 00:00:21.693
We are in Table view, on the Shipments table.

6
00:00:21.693 --> 00:00:23.889
Look at the Order Status column:

7
00:00:23.889 --> 00:00:25.719
Delivered, Shipped, Cancelled, and more.

8
00:00:25.719 --> 00:00:28.280
We want to flag the cancelled orders.

9
00:00:49.900 --> 00:00:54.183
On the Logic page of our report, we will later show the results.

10
00:00:54.183 --> 00:00:56.160
For now, let's build the column.

11
00:01:19.900 --> 00:01:25.180
Back in Table view, select the Shipments table, and on Table tools, click New column.

12
00:01:49.900 --> 00:01:53.514
I start typing the name and the result text. But wait:

13
00:01:53.514 --> 00:01:56.800
first the name, then the equals sign, then the formula.

14
00:02:15.900 --> 00:02:16.962
I type IF.

15
00:02:16.962 --> 00:02:18.732
The tooltip shows three parts:

16
00:02:18.732 --> 00:02:22.980
a logical test, the value if true, and the value if false.

17
00:02:27.900 --> 00:02:28.677
The test:

18
00:02:28.677 --> 00:02:31.396
Shipments, Order Status, equals Cancelled, in quotes.

19
00:02:31.396 --> 00:02:34.504
Then a comma, and the value if true:

20
00:02:34.504 --> 00:02:38.000
Ask Reason for Cancelled Order Status, also in quotes.

21
00:02:55.900 --> 00:02:59.304
Then a comma, and the value if false: It is okay.

22
00:02:59.304 --> 00:03:01.780
I name the column Reason and press Enter.

23
00:03:17.900 --> 00:03:19.404
Now open the filter on the Reason column.

24
00:03:19.404 --> 00:03:20.156
It shows two values:

25
00:03:20.156 --> 00:03:22.600
Ask Reason for Cancelled Order Status, and It is okay. Our IF works!

